{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347455-zqdg6AEpAkbtSQjYNrJW","role":"assistant","created":1775347461,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Treasury Bulletin doesn't contain detailed historical data for personal saving rates between 1950-1990. It only provides information about the recent rates (1987-1991) and mentions a long-term average of 6.7%. \n\nLet me search more broadly for historical data in the document. Perhaps there's a table somewhere with yearly data.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_26ffb5bb5edc4c30aeea0a23","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1991_09.json') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Look for tables with years and percentages - search for year ranges\nfor i, elem in enumerate(data['document']['elements']):\n    content = str(elem.get('content', ''))\n    # Look for multiple year rows in a table with percentage values  \n    if '<table>' in content:\n        # Check if this has year data from 1950-1990 range\n        years_found = [y for y in range(1950, 1991) if str(y) in content]\n        if len(years_found) >= 5:\n            print(f'Element {i}: Years={years_found}')\n            print(content[:800])\n            print('---')\n\" 2>/dev/null | head -50"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
