nt peak in the mid-1970s, with rates reaching as high as 10-11% during that period. While I can't confirm the exact peak year with my current documents, the evidence points to 1974 as a likely candidate.\n\nHistorical saving rate data indicates variations across different decades, with notable peaks around 1974-1975 and another significant increase in the early 1980s. The context of the question suggests focusing on the 1950-1990 timeframe, which aligns with these historical trends.\n\nThe peak appears to be around 1974 or 1975, with rates climbing to 9-11% during the oil crisis period. This corresponds with economic literature on saving rates, particularly during the high inflation years of the 1970s.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_5d7162f0e033488c96ce8b43","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"wc -l /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1991_09.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
